# Copy to `.env` and fill in values. Do not commit real secrets.
#
# Loading:
# - `devenv shell` / `devenv processes start` source `.env` automatically
#   (see devenv.nix). Restart the app after changing values.
# - Outside devenv: `set -a && source .env && set +a` then start the server.
#
# Self-check (prints provider names only, never secrets):
#   mix run --no-start -e 'IO.inspect(Manifold.Connectors.configured_providers())'
# Expect ["gmail"] and/or ["microsoft"] when credentials are visible to the process.
#
# Mail-client-style OAuth (same UX idea as Apple Mail / Thunderbird):
# register YOUR OWN public/native OAuth app, then set only client_id below.
# Do NOT copy Apple Mail, Outlook, or any other vendor's client_id — that
# violates provider ToS and redirect/device registration will not match.

# Required for production releases (optional in MIX_ENV=dev; a non-prod
# key is already set in config/dev.exs). Base64 of exactly 32 random bytes:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# MANIFOLD_CONNECTOR_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Gmail: client_id only (recommended) ---
# Google device flow does NOT allow Gmail API scopes. Gmail uses
# authorization code + PKCE with a redirect URI (browser sign-in).
# Prefer Google Cloud → OAuth client type "Desktop app" so you only need:
# MANIFOLD_GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=your-desktop-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
# MANIFOLD_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=   # leave unset for Desktop/public clients
#
# Web application clients may include a secret; still optional in Manifold:
# MANIFOLD_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional HTTPS overrides (defaults are Google production endpoints):
# MANIFOLD_GMAIL_AUTHORIZATION_URL=https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth
# MANIFOLD_GMAIL_TOKEN_URL=https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token
# MANIFOLD_GMAIL_USERINFO_URL=https://openidconnect.googleapis.com/v1/userinfo
# MANIFOLD_GMAIL_API_BASE_URL=https://gmail.googleapis.com

# --- Microsoft 365: client_id only (recommended) ---
# Uses OAuth Device Authorization Grant (public client). Enable
# "Allow public client flows" on the Entra app. No redirect URI required.
# MANIFOLD_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# MANIFOLD_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=   # leave unset for public clients
# Work/school default. Use a tenant GUID/domain for a single tenant, or
# "common" only if personal Microsoft accounts must be allowed.
# MANIFOLD_MICROSOFT_TENANT=organizations
# Optional HTTPS overrides (defaults derive from the tenant):
# MANIFOLD_MICROSOFT_DEVICE_CODE_URL=
# MANIFOLD_MICROSOFT_TOKEN_URL=
# MANIFOLD_MICROSOFT_API_BASE_URL=https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0

# Local Gmail OAuth callback (register this exact URI with Google when using
# a Web client; Desktop clients use the loopback URL Manifold generates):
#   http://localhost:4290/connectors/gmail/callback
